&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think rigorously; act quickly.&lt;/strong&gt; We reason from first principles, then act rather than debate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Know yourself and grow.&lt;/strong&gt; We own our imperfections and seek feedback to grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accept reality. Propose solutions.&lt;/strong&gt; We focus on what can change and bring solutions, not just problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be productively ambitious.&lt;/strong&gt; We take risks for step-change impact, not incremental progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If they describe how you like to work and they energize you, this could be a great fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Want to learn more? Read and listen:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are one of&lt;a href=&quot;https://time.com/collection/time100-most-influential-companies/2026/givedirectly/&quot;&gt; Time100’s&lt;/a&gt; Most Influential Companies of 2026, and our work has been covered by&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.economist.com/special-report/2024/01/10/givedirectly-does-what-it-says-on-the-tin&quot;&gt; The Economist&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.npr.org/sections/goatsandsoda/2023/12/07/1217478771/its-one-of-the-biggest-experiments-in-fighting-global-poverty-now-the-results-ar&quot;&gt; NPR&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ted.com/talks/rory_stewart_to_end_extreme_poverty_give_cash_not_advice&quot;&gt; TED&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/washingtonpost-apr-2024/&quot;&gt; The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;. We&#39;re now preparing to deliver billions of dollars a year to people in extreme poverty, if funding allows. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/deliver-billions&quot;&gt;Read our CEO&#39;s essay&lt;/a&gt; on what that will take.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt; Head of People&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level:&lt;/strong&gt; Director&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Remote, but in a location that allows for at least ~3 hours of daily overlap with East Africa Time, and meaningful overlap with US Eastern hours.&amp;nbsp;At this stage of GiveDirectly’s growth and scale, we’re prioritizing hiring in the countries below, where we can employ you through a GD entity or an established employer of record: Cameroon, Canada, Colombia, DRC, Germany, Ghana, Kenya, Malawi, Mozambique, Netherlands, Nigeria, Poland, Portugal, Rwanda, South Africa, Spain, Turkey, Uganda, United Kingdom, and United States. This list reflects where our employment infrastructure is established today, and may evolve as we grow. If you’re based elsewhere and not open to relocation, we may not be able to consider your application for this role right now, but we’d encourage you to check back. &lt;em&gt;Please note that we are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of employment Visas in the U.S. or U.K. at this time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Approximately 3-4 trips per year, including at least one to a country of operation and one to a key in-person leadership moment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently planning for a significant increase in scale, and we are building the People function that can carry it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is our first senior talent management role. Today we have pieces of talent management programs and processes in place, but not yet a function. You will build one: an intentional approach to how we onboard, develop, and retain our people. That covers performance management and its link to pay, manager and leadership development, learning, onboarding, talent planning and succession, employee listening and engagement, and culture and values.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The first year is weighted toward four priorities: joining the redesign of our performance system early, alongside the Head of People, and owning it as it moves into execution, as we move to pay for performance, revamping onboarding ahead of our next wave of hiring, planning our values retreat for senior leaders, and getting a read on employee listening and engagement. As those take shape, the balance shifts toward the longer-term build: the vision and roadmap for the function, a foundational manager program, talent planning and succession, and the team around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reason for this weight: the performance system and onboarding are our most acute gaps today, but they should not be construed as a ceiling of the job. We are hiring a senior talent management leader who can shape the whole function over several years, not the owner of one or two programs. If your instinct on reading this is that the performance redesign is the whole job, this role probably isn’t the right fit, and the reverse is also true: if you want to set strategy but not build the first versions yourself, year one will frustrate you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Build the talent management function&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your first 90 days, assess what exists today across these areas, recommend the sequencing for the first year, and agree to it with the Head of People.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the vision and multi-year roadmap for talent management across the areas it covers, and sequence the work against the People roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose the team around it, and decide what we build in-house and what we buy or borrow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect talent management to workforce planning, compensation, and recruitment, in partnership with the Head of People, Finance, and function leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an approach to talent and succession planning, starting with critical roles: work with leaders to identify succession gaps, assess potential successors, and put development plans in place to prepare people for future opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Own the performance system&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join the performance system redesign early, alongside the Head of People, and own it as it moves into execution: a system that produces reliable, calibrated outputs to inform merit increases, connected to our new salary bands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make the system worth using, not a check-the-box exercise: one that helps managers hold better performance and development conversations and gives employees clarity on expectations, feedback, and growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build calibration and the data around it so ratings and merit decisions stay consistent and fair across countries, currencies, and manager quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a clear global standard for handling low performance that doesn’t default to a misconduct process, and equip managers to use it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the performance system helps managers identify and support sustained high performance, connecting it to recognition, development, and career growth opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Iterate the system through multiple cycles, using calibration, outcome data, and feedback from managers and employees to improve it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Build how people join, learn, and are led&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Revamp onboarding ahead of our next wave of hiring: own the content and experience for new hires and their managers, working with People Ops on process and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a foundational manager program and the tools behind it: feedback, coaching, difficult conversations, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend into leadership development and broader learning as the function matures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Shape culture and listen to employees&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan the values retreat with an external facilitator and our executive sponsor, and own what carries into daily work afterward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get a read on listening and engagement today, covering what we hear, where it goes, and what should change, and use it to build our employee listening strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What this role is not&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not a recruiting role. Hiring sits with our Talent Acquisition team. You partner with them on the handoff into onboarding and on how we assess and develop talent once people are here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not the owner of compensation design. Pay structures and bands are set through our compensation work. You own how performance is assessed and how ratings connect to pay decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not an employee relations or casework role. Cases in country belong to managers and HR Managers, supported by the People team. You own the performance system and the manager capability that helps them handle concerns well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Required&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in talent management, performance, or organizational design roles, including time leading a function or a major part of one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a hands-on builder who has deep experience building talent management programs and systems (e.g. onboarding, manager development, performance, employee listening, etc.) from scratch in a start-up or scale-up environment &lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt; for a bifurcated, global workforce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have built programs and content people actually used, and can show how you knew they worked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think in systems and use data (survey, performance, calibration) to make decisions. You can show how a change in one part of a talent system, such as ratings, calibration, pay, promotion, or onboarding, shows up in the others, and you reason from the underlying problem rather than copying another organization’s template.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You design with change management in mind from the start. You plan for how managers and employees in different countries and cultures will adopt a new program or system as part of the design, not as a rollout step afterward, and can show how you knew it stuck rather than being worked around.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have had exposure to compensation design or worked closely with a total rewards team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated judgment and prioritization chops and experience influencing without authority.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Preferred&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have designed a performance system linked to pay decisions, not only administered one.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a mission-driven or international organization, ideally alongside high-growth commercial or tech experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across countries in sub-Saharan Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with external facilitators, consultants, or vendors, and knowing what to hand off and what to hold.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional French or Portuguese.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At GiveDirectly, we strive to pay our employees generously and equitably. We use an accredited third party salary aggregator to calculate what we believe to be competitive pay based on role, location, and cost of living. We also have a no negotiation policy to ensure we are paying staff equitably across roles. Unless otherwise noted, the benefits stipend may be used to cover benefits or taken as additional taxable income. If you are in a location other than those listed below, our recruiters will share compensation information during your initial screen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;United States&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base Salary: $134,400&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Annual Benefits Stipend: $21,393&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus Target: 15%&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;United Kingdom&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base Salary: £94,605&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Annual Benefits Stipend: £2,760&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus Target: 15%&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Kenya&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base Salary: $106,282&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Annual Benefits Stipend: $8,453&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bonus Target: 15%&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at GiveDirectly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GiveDirectly is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants are considered for employment without regard to the person’s race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flagging for US applicants:&lt;/em&gt; We invite you to &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://app.getguru.com/card/TrxrEknc/US-Federal-Law-on-Workplace-Discrimination&quot;&gt;Know Your Rights&lt;/a&gt;&quot; as an applicant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to Safeguarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a global organization working with communities to eliminate extreme poverty, GiveDirectly takes the safeguarding of its recipients, staff, and partners seriously. To that end, GiveDirectly is a member of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://misconduct-disclosure-scheme.org/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://misconduct-disclosure-scheme.org/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Misconduct Disclosure Scheme&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;, and will systematically check with previous employers about any abuse or misconduct related matters involving potential new hires. We may also employ other robust pre-hire screens, including in-depth reference checks, criminal background checks, and sanctions screens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These efforts help us continue to build and maintain trust with the communities we work with, and prevent abuse to our recipients and staff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;**GD is committed to observing all local, national and international laws that protect people and basic human rights of all. GD is committed to a policy of “zero tolerance when it comes to preventing,&amp;nbsp; reporting, or responding to any form of abuse or&amp;nbsp; exploitation.” and expects anyone who works for GD to uphold the protection and safeguarding of our recipients as a priority.**&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reasonable Accommodations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to fostering an inclusive and accessible work environment. If you require any accommodations during the application or interview process, or to perform the essential functions of the role, please email us at careers@givedirectly.org with the email subject “Accommodation Needed”. We will work with you to ensure reasonable accommodations are made to support your needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;il&quot;&gt;Want to put your best foot forward on your GiveDirectly application?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;il&quot;&gt; Take a look at our &lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JRyU81RnTGHQrw9nHTPw7oe_urTDh9JT/view?usp=sharing&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Application Prep Guide&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About GiveDirectly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What if the most effective way to fight poverty was also the simplest: give people money and trust them to decide what they need?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since 2011, GiveDirectly has proven that idea at scale. We’ve delivered more than $1B in cash directly to 2+ million people living in poverty and crisis across 15 countries, and rigorous research shows the results: healthier kids, stronger businesses, sturdier homes, and more resilient families and local economies. Cash is now widely recognized as one of the most scalable, cost-effective, and dignified forms of aid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ambition goes beyond our own programs. We want cash to become the benchmark for aid, much as the index fund became the benchmark for investing, so that every aid dollar is held to one question: &lt;em&gt;is this doing more good than giving the money directly to people living in poverty?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re growing fast, and this is a rare and important moment to join.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect to hit $1B in revenue in 2026 with significant growth forecast for 2027. At the same time we are building a new technology stack and operating model designed for a roughly 10x change in scale, and we are actively pursuing partnerships with major funders to move even more money in bigger ways, to people who need it. We are known for our extensive integration of technology into field processes; our quantitative approach to performance measurement; and our commitment to rigorous, independent, experimental evaluation of our impact, with multiple Randomized Control Trials completed and others in progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team spans 20+ countries and 69 languages. Our culture is candid, analytical, and non-hierarchical. We expect high ownership and give people real responsibility early. Our values are central to how we hire, work, and grow, and they are deliberately opinionated:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipients first.&lt;/strong&gt; Recipients’ preferences come before those of donors or ourselves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team next.&lt;/strong&gt; We optimize for organizational success, not individual success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be proactively candid.&lt;/strong&gt; We say what we believe and share information openly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create positive energy.&lt;/strong&gt; We aim to be a source of energy for colleagues, not a drain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think rigorously; act quickly.&lt;/strong&gt; We reason from first principles, then act rather than debate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Know yourself and grow.&lt;/strong&gt; We own our imperfections and seek feedback to grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accept reality. Propose solutions.&lt;/strong&gt; We focus on what can change and bring solutions, not just problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be productively ambitious.&lt;/strong&gt; We take risks for step-change impact, not incremental progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If they describe how you like to work and they energize you, this could be a great fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Want to learn more? Read and listen:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are one of&lt;a href=&quot;https://time.com/collection/time100-most-influential-companies/2026/givedirectly/&quot;&gt; Time100’s&lt;/a&gt; Most Influential Companies of 2026, and our work has been covered by&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.economist.com/special-report/2024/01/10/givedirectly-does-what-it-says-on-the-tin&quot;&gt; The Economist&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.npr.org/sections/goatsandsoda/2023/12/07/1217478771/its-one-of-the-biggest-experiments-in-fighting-global-poverty-now-the-results-ar&quot;&gt; NPR&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ted.com/talks/rory_stewart_to_end_extreme_poverty_give_cash_not_advice&quot;&gt; TED&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/washingtonpost-apr-2024/&quot;&gt; The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;. We&#39;re now preparing to deliver billions of dollars a year to people in extreme poverty, if funding allows. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/deliver-billions&quot;&gt;Read our CEO&#39;s essay&lt;/a&gt; on what that will take.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Internal Audit Field Officer will play a critical day-to-day role in ensuring that GiveDirectly is able to deliver cash transfers to recipients safely. The Field Officer will be part of the team that is responsible for preventing, detecting, mitigating, and investigating field-based risks for GiveDirectly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will reward high-quality judgment on operational questions and challenges, a strong work ethic, effective communication skills, attention to detail, a strong sense of independence, and a strong commitment to GiveDirectly’s mission and model. In essence, the Internal Audit Field Officer will be expected to audit the work of the enrolment team, whose core responsibility is surveying households and enrolling them in our programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the sensitive nature of the work done by the internal audit team, we require all in-country internal audit staff to remain firewalled from the rest of the staff. This means operating discretely and independently, with interactions strictly limited to just the colleagues within the same team. The role holder will be expected to carry out day-to-day audit tasks with an absolute level of discretion, impartiality, neutrality, and independence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duty Station: Magarini Sub-County&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fresh graduates are highly encouraged to apply.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipient engagement (60%):&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct in-person household visits for all individuals selected for enrollment to check and determine their safety for enrollment, assess vulnerabilities, and flag any pre-enrollment risk indicators to the management for proactive resolution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly engage with high-risk recipients to provide them with the necessary support so that they receive their transfers safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly engage with recipients to identify any corrections or improvements in field processes that are needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and resolve any recipient cases that have been flagged to the Internal Audit team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and escalate key risks associated with GD’s programs in the community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk monitoring (30%):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the IA AFM to undertake risk monitoring activities within the community&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the IA AFM to verify the quality and the risk level of the partner data pre-enrollment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure the quality of data received from the field teams against set data quality standards, reporting any cases of inconsistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report any cases of fraud and bribery by GD staff and or recipient(s) that are identified through the appropriate escalation channels.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilise technology to flag any abnormalities in operation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other (10%)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the IA AFM in the onboarding processes of new team members&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the IA AFM with hosting visitors to the project location&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with response to “crisis” events (e.g., refusal spikes, government shutdown, coordinated fraud, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote effective team culture by encouraging recognition of positive achievements, planning team events periodically, and other team-building initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelors degree in Social Sciences, Development Studies, or a related field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Having a Fraud Investigation experience is an added advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has the ability to audit cash transfer recipients by conducting in-person or virtual surveys and associated processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in &lt;strong&gt;Giriama&lt;/strong&gt; language is&lt;strong&gt; a MUST.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English and Kiswahili&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good computer and mobile device data entry and assessment ability or experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess critical thinking ability and good judgment in resolving operational glitches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possesses a high-quality problem-solving work ethic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good time-management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in the mission of GiveDirectly and commitment to advancing GD’s distinctive values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical fitness and the ability to cope with difficult weather conditions or terrain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to exercise patience and good judgment in resolving recipient problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at GiveDirectly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GiveDirectly is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants are considered for employment without regard to the person’s race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flagging for US applicants:&lt;/em&gt; We invite you to &quot;&lt;a href=&quot;https://app.getguru.com/card/TrxrEknc/US-Federal-Law-on-Workplace-Discrimination&quot;&gt;Know Your Rights&lt;/a&gt;&quot; as an applicant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to Safeguarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a global organization working with communities to eliminate extreme poverty, GiveDirectly takes the safeguarding of its recipients, staff, and partners seriously. To that end, GiveDirectly is a member of the&amp;nbsp;&lt;u data-stringify-type=&quot;underline&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://misconduct-disclosure-scheme.org/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://misconduct-disclosure-scheme.org/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Misconduct Disclosure Scheme&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/u&gt;, and will systematically check with previous employers about any abuse or misconduct related matters involving potential new hires. We may also employ other robust pre-hire screens, including in-depth reference checks, criminal background checks, and sanctions screens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These efforts help us continue to build and maintain trust with the communities we work with, and prevent abuse to our recipients and staff.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;**GD is committed to observing all local, national and international laws that protect people and basic human rights of all. GD is committed to a policy of “zero tolerance when it comes to preventing,&amp;nbsp; reporting, or responding to any form of abuse or&amp;nbsp; exploitation.” and expects anyone who works for GD to uphold the protection and safeguarding of our recipients as a priority.**&lt;/p&gt;
