&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About GiveDirectly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What if the most effective way to fight poverty was also the simplest: give people money and trust them to decide what they need?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since 2011, GiveDirectly has proven that idea at scale. We’ve delivered more than $1B in cash directly to 2+ million people living in poverty and crisis across 15 countries, and rigorous research shows the results: healthier kids, stronger businesses, sturdier homes, and more resilient families and local economies. Cash is now widely recognized as one of the most scalable, cost-effective, and dignified forms of aid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ambition goes beyond our own programs. We want cash to become the benchmark for aid, much as the index fund became the benchmark for investing, so that every aid dollar is held to one question: &lt;em&gt;is this doing more good than giving the money directly to people living in poverty?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re growing fast, and this is a rare and important moment to join.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect to hit $1B in revenue in 2026 with significant growth forecast for 2027. At the same time we are building a new technology stack and operating model designed for a roughly 10x change in scale, and we are actively pursuing partnerships with major funders to move even more money in bigger ways, to people who need it. We are known for our extensive integration of technology into field processes; our quantitative approach to performance measurement; and our commitment to rigorous, independent, experimental evaluation of our impact, with multiple Randomized Control Trials completed and others in progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team spans 20+ countries and 69 languages. Our culture is candid, analytical, and non-hierarchical. We expect high ownership and give people real responsibility early. Our values are central to how we hire, work, and grow, and they are deliberately opinionated:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recipients first.&lt;/strong&gt; Recipients’ preferences come before those of donors or ourselves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team next.&lt;/strong&gt; We optimize for organizational success, not individual success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be proactively candid.&lt;/strong&gt; We say what we believe and share information openly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create positive energy.&lt;/strong&gt; We aim to be a source of energy for colleagues, not a drain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think rigorously; act quickly.&lt;/strong&gt; We reason from first principles, then act rather than debate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Know yourself and grow.&lt;/strong&gt; We own our imperfections and seek feedback to grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accept reality. Propose solutions.&lt;/strong&gt; We focus on what can change and bring solutions, not just problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be productively ambitious.&lt;/strong&gt; We take risks for step-change impact, not incremental progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If they describe how you like to work and they energize you, this could be a great fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Want to learn more? Read and listen:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are one of&lt;a href=&quot;https://time.com/collection/time100-most-influential-companies/2026/givedirectly/&quot;&gt; Time100’s&lt;/a&gt; Most Influential Companies of 2026, and our work has been covered by&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.economist.com/special-report/2024/01/10/givedirectly-does-what-it-says-on-the-tin&quot;&gt; The Economist&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.npr.org/sections/goatsandsoda/2023/12/07/1217478771/its-one-of-the-biggest-experiments-in-fighting-global-poverty-now-the-results-ar&quot;&gt; NPR&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ted.com/talks/rory_stewart_to_end_extreme_poverty_give_cash_not_advice&quot;&gt; TED&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/washingtonpost-apr-2024/&quot;&gt; The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;. We&#39;re now preparing to deliver billions of dollars a year to people in extreme poverty, if funding allows. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/deliver-billions&quot;&gt;Read our CEO&#39;s essay&lt;/a&gt; on what that will take.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About GiveDirectly in the DRC&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GiveDirectly DRC was established in 2018 to enable cash transfers to poor and rural populations via mobile phones, thereby promoting food security, poverty reduction, and financial inclusion. We aimed to demonstrate the operational feasibility and cost-effectiveness of transferring large volumes of money digitally in one of the world&#39;s least developed countries. Since its inception four years ago, GiveDirectly DRC has used mobile phones to transfer over $14 million to more than 65,000 beneficiaries in four provinces: South Kivu, North Kivu, Ituri, and Kinshasa.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GiveDirectly&#39;s activities in the DRC have expanded to include, among other things: compelling proofs of concept for mobile-based cash transfers; and the implementation of innovative technologies to target disadvantaged urban populations in Kinshasa, in collaboration with the DRC&#39;s social protection agency, the DRC Social Fund. The delivery of contactless cash to beneficiaries in Beni and Bunia affected by the economic consequences of COVID-19. You will be joining Give Directly DRC at an exciting time in its history, as we are establishing and hope to launch several new programs and strengthen our partnership with the DRC government.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Manager, Operations (DRC), you&#39;ll build and lead the operational backbone behind GiveDirectly&#39;s programs in the country. You&#39;ll direct the support services team end-to-end — HR, logistics, procurement, and administration — while managing a team of managers. You&#39;ll design a procurement strategy that keeps goods and services flowing efficiently and reliably across provinces, own fleet and logistics management as the program scales, and manage the operational budget with an eye for efficiency. You&#39;ll also support the Country Director on HR strategy — recruitment, training, and performance — and design the systems needed for a much larger footprint across provinces, from procurement to digital tools that improve scalability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who can build systems as readily as they can lead people, and who&#39;s energized by both strategic design and the operational details that make it real on the ground.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the DRC support services team end-to-end — HR, logistics, procurement, administration, and office management — including direct oversight of managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and drive a procurement strategy ensuring efficient, compliant, and resilient sourcing across provinces, and own fleet and logistics management as the program scales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the operational budget, forecasting and driving efficiency across procurement, logistics, and administrative spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Country Director on HR strategy — recruitment, training, performance management, and talent density — through oversight of the HR function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design systems and processes to support a much larger footprint across provinces, anticipating future needs and identifying AI and digital opportunities to improve scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop support services managers to build operational excellence beyond individual contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a compliance and operational risk register, and lead internal spot checks, audit preparedness, and action plans in partnership with Finance and Internal Audit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own donor reporting, budget tracking, and donor visit coordination, and serve as the primary point of contact between the Country Office and GSS on operational and compliance matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Operational Knowledge Base and lead onboarding, training, and localization of materials as the team grows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (management, administration, finance, or related); a master&#39;s degree is an asset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 6 years of experience in operations management, with a track record of transforming informal systems into structured, compliant, and scalable ones, including direct oversight of managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial and budget management skills, with experience managing an operational budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience maintaining a risk register and working closely with internal/external audit functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and coaching managers, with comfort delegating execution while retaining accountability for results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong digital fluency, with experience using and training teams on multiple platforms (Google Suite, Salesforce, Asana, Guru, Slack)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with international NGO standards and donor compliance frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating the DRC&#39;s complex legal environment, including labor law and immigration requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong alignment with &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/givedirectly-values&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GiveDirectly&#39;s values&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and oral communication skills, including ability to communicate fluently in English and French with high level stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional proficiency in French and English required; knowledge of Congolese Swahili and/or Lingala is an asset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At GiveDirectly, we strive to pay our employees generously and equitably. We use an accredited third party salary aggregator to calculate what we believe to be competitive pay based on role, location, and cost of living. We also have a no negotiation policy to ensure we are paying staff equitably across roles. Read more about our compensation philosophy&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://drive.google.com/file/d/1onxCdQX_DacG0812Wr99LF6zlMTg7RTP/view?usp=sharing&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unless otherwise noted, the benefits stipend may be used to cover benefits or taken as additional taxable income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;344&quot; data-end=&quot;371&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;344&quot; data-end=&quot;360&quot;&gt;Base Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; $94,500&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;374&quot; data-end=&quot;559&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;374&quot; data-end=&quot;406&quot;&gt;Bonus at Target Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; 10% (~$9,450, with potential for upside. For reference, with the organization’s current performance multiplier, this amount would be $11,057 in 2025)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;562&quot; data-end=&quot;617&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;562&quot; data-end=&quot;615&quot;&gt;Estimated Total Compensation at Target: $103,950+&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is onsite in Goma, DRC. We welcome candidates based in the DRC as well as those willing to relocate to be based in the DRC.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
