&lt;p&gt;We are one of&lt;a href=&quot;https://time.com/collection/time100-most-influential-companies/2026/givedirectly/&quot;&gt; Time100’s&lt;/a&gt; Most Influential Companies of 2026, and our work has been covered by&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.economist.com/special-report/2024/01/10/givedirectly-does-what-it-says-on-the-tin&quot;&gt; The Economist&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.npr.org/sections/goatsandsoda/2023/12/07/1217478771/its-one-of-the-biggest-experiments-in-fighting-global-poverty-now-the-results-ar&quot;&gt; NPR&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ted.com/talks/rory_stewart_to_end_extreme_poverty_give_cash_not_advice&quot;&gt; TED&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/washingtonpost-apr-2024/&quot;&gt; The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;. We&#39;re now preparing to deliver billions of dollars a year to people in extreme poverty, if funding allows. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/deliver-billions&quot;&gt;Read our CEO&#39;s essay&lt;/a&gt; on what that will take.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you an experienced engineer at the stage of your career where, above all, you want to do good?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is about using engineering to support fundraising: delighting our donors; helping our fundraisers; getting donations recorded and safely started on their journey to our recipients; telling donors and the public about what happens to their gifts. A bit of website development. A lot of plumbing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The good news about &lt;em&gt;this&lt;/em&gt; position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will make a difference to people in extreme poverty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will work independently, with few constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will work directly with lovely people from across our fundraising teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The trade-offs:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;There is only one other fundraising engineer and mostly you will be working on your own&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our technology is a mixture of boring (Laravel, PHP, plain JS, HTML and CSS) and legacy (Salesforce, Wordpress, wrangling CSV files sent by our partners)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We&#39;re growing, but this is a role for someone who values depth and impact over a fast title ladder.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The maybe good maybe bad news about the role depending on who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are all in on AI where it allows us to get more $ to people in extreme poverty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want a role where you will be part of a bigger engineering team, working in Python or working on more complex tasks, then please take a look at our &lt;a href=&quot;https://job-boards.greenhouse.io/givedirectly/jobs/4558344005&quot;&gt;other engineering roles&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is right for you if:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about our mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You agree with &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.givedirectly.org/givedirectly-values&quot;&gt;our values&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have the right to work in one of the countries we&#39;re able to hire from (you can check the current list &lt;a href=&quot;https://perfectwiki.page/p/iOeyfUha_9&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re happy working remotely, and taking meetings across East Africa Time and US Eastern Time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are happy to travel to meet your colleagues in the US, Europe and Africa a few weeks a year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are fluent in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 4+ years of engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re happy working autonomously: defining what needs doing, doing it, getting it tested and launched, fixing the bugs, and hustling to make progress every day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re comfortable being on-call on peak donation days (Giving Tuesday and the last weeks of the year), including owning an incident: working out what matters, communicating with fundraisers, and debugging on legacy and others&#39; code, sometimes when no other engineers are available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are happy with our boring and legacy technologies (Laravel, PHP, plain JS, HTML, CSS, Salesforce, Wordpress, SQL, wrangling csv files etc). You don’t have to be experienced in all of them, but you do have to be genuinely happy to use them (many engineers are not…).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are happy and skilled at working directly with non-engineers on messy, poorly defined, rapidly changing, sometimes boring tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
